2025-05-02 04:44:38 - ThreadPoolExecutor-0_9 - INFO - [Exploration]
```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a few raw track durations (in milliseconds) to get a feeling for the data.
SELECT DISTINCT "Milliseconds"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show the same durations converted to minutes (ms ÷ 60 000).
SELECT DISTINCT 
       "TrackId",
       ROUND("Milliseconds" / 60000.0, 2) AS "Minutes"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Classify each track as Short (<3 min), Medium (3–5 min) or Long (>5 min).
SELECT DISTINCT 
       "TrackId",
       CASE 
            WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'Short'
            WHEN "Milliseconds" < 300000 THEN 'Medium'
            ELSE 'Long'
       END                AS "LengthCategory"
FROM "Track"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Count how many tracks fall into every length‑category.
SELECT 
       CASE 
            WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'Short'
            WHEN "Milliseconds" < 300000 THEN 'Medium'
            ELSE 'Long'
       END                AS "LengthCategory",
       COUNT(*)           AS "TrackCount"
FROM "Track"
GROUP BY "LengthCategory";
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Look at a few invoice‑lines to confirm price * quantity is the sales value.
SELECT DISTINCT 
       "InvoiceLineId",
       "TrackId",
       "UnitPrice",
       "Quantity",
       ROUND("UnitPrice" * "Quantity", 2) AS "LineRevenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Aggregate total revenue per track (summing all its invoice‑lines).
SELECT 
       "TrackId",
       ROUND(SUM("UnitPrice" * "Quantity"), 2) AS "TrackRevenue"
FROM "InvoiceLine"
GROUP BY "TrackId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Join tracks with their invoice‑lines and roll revenue up into length‑categories.
SELECT 
       CASE 
            WHEN t."Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'Short'
            WHEN t."Milliseconds" < 300000 THEN 'Medium'
            ELSE 'Long'
       END                             AS "LengthCategory",
       ROUND(SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity"), 2) AS "TotalRevenue"
FROM "Track"        AS t
JOIN "InvoiceLine"  AS il ON il."TrackId" = t."TrackId"
GROUP BY "LengthCategory";
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Final answer – for each length‑category return the minimum & maximum duration
--               (in minutes) of tracks in that category and the total revenue generated by them.
SELECT 
       cat."LengthCategory",
       ROUND(MIN(cat."DurationMinutes"), 2) AS "MinMinutes",
       ROUND(MAX(cat."DurationMinutes"), 2) AS "MaxMinutes",
       ROUND(SUM(il."UnitPrice" * il."Quantity"), 2) AS "TotalRevenue"
FROM (
       SELECT 
              "TrackId",
              ("Milliseconds" / 60000.0)                                AS "DurationMinutes",
              CASE
                   WHEN "Milliseconds" < 180000 THEN 'Short'
                   WHEN "Milliseconds" < 300000 THEN 'Medium'
                   ELSE 'Long'
              END                                                       AS "LengthCategory"
       FROM "Track"
)                      AS cat
JOIN "InvoiceLine"     AS il ON il."TrackId" = cat."TrackId"
GROUP BY cat."LengthCategory";
```

These eight queries progress from simple exploration of durations to the complete report requested: minimum and maximum time (in minutes) and total sales revenue for each Short, Medium, and Long track category.
